  "severity": "important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-114946:\n\tVulnerability in the OpenJDK hotspot/compiler component.\n\nCVE-2026-114945:\n\tVulnerability in the OpenJDK core-libs/java.lang component.\n\nCVE-2026-114944:\n\tVulnerability in the OpenJDK core-svc/java.lang.management component.\n\nCVE-2026-114943:\n\tVulnerability in the OpenJDK hotspot/runtime component.\n\nCVE-2026-114942:\n\tVulnerability in the OpenJDK core-libs component.\n\nCVE-2026-114940:\n\tVulnerability in the OpenJDK security-libs/javax.net.ssl component.\n\nCVE-2026-114939:\n\tVulnerability in the OpenJDK security-libs/org.ietf.jgss component.\n\nCVE-2026-114938:\n\tA memory-corruption vulnerability exists in the OpenJDK Base64 decoder affecting OpenJDK 17.0.6 and later on x86-64 systems with specific CPU capabilities. ARM64 systems are not affected. Depending on the deployment context, exploitation could result in a JVM crash for unauthenticated users or, in certain application environments, code execution by an authenticated low-privileged user. Oracle has issued a patch covering versions 17, 21, 25, and 27.\n",
